diff --git a/features/todo-editing.feature b/features/todo-editing.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..9a9d8ad
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/todo-editing.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,53 @@
+Feature: Todo item editing
+  As a user
+  I want to edit existing todo items
+  So that I can update my task descriptions
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app has loaded
+    And a todo with title "Buy groceries" exists
+
+  Scenario: User enters edit mode by double-clicking a todo label
+    When the user double-clicks the label for "Buy groceries"
+    Then the todo item "Buy groceries" has class "editing"
+    And the edit input is visible and focused
+    And the edit input contains "Buy groceries"
+
+  Scenario: User saves an edit by pressing Enter
+    When the user double-clicks the label for "Buy groceries"
+    And the user types "Buy organic groceries" into the edit input
+    And presses Enter
+    Then the todo item "Buy groceries" is updated to "Buy organic groceries"
+    And the todo item "Buy groceries" does not have class "editing"
+
+  Scenario: User saves an edit by blurring the input
+    When the user double-clicks the label for "Buy groceries"
+    And the user types "Buy organic groceries" into the edit input
+    And the edit input loses focus
+    Then the todo item "Buy groceries" is updated to "Buy organic groceries"
+    And the todo item "Buy groceries" does not have class "editing"
+
+  Scenario: User discards an edit by pressing Escape
+    When the user double-clicks the label for "Buy groceries"
+    And the user types "Buy organic groceries" into the edit input
+    And presses Escape
+    Then the todo item title remains "Buy groceries"
+    And the todo item "Buy groceries" does not have class "editing"
+
+  Scenario: User clears an item by editing to empty text
+    When the user double-clicks the label for "Buy groceries"
+    And the user clears the edit input
+    And presses Enter
+    Then the todo list does not contain "Buy groceries"
+
+  Scenario: User clears an item by editing to whitespace-only text
+    When the user double-clicks the label for "Buy groceries"
+    And the user types "   " into the edit input
+    And presses Enter
+    Then the todo list does not contain "Buy groceries"
+
+  Scenario: Todo title is trimmed on save
+    When the user double-clicks the label for "Buy groceries"
+    And the user types "  Buy organic groceries  " into the edit input
+    And presses Enter
+    Then the todo item "Buy groceries" is updated to "Buy organic groceries"
\ No newline at end of file
diff --git a/features/todo-management.feature b/features/todo-management.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..e84efe5
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/todo-management.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,58 @@
+Feature: Todo item management
+  As a user
+  I want to add, view, and track todo items
+  So that I can manage my task list
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded fresh
+
+  Scenario: App shows input field and hides main and footer when there are no todos
+    Given the app has loaded
+    Then the new-todo input field is visible
+    And the main section is not visible
+    And the footer is not visible
+
+  Scenario: User adds a new todo by pressing Enter
+    Given the app has loaded
+    When the user types "Buy groceries" into the new-todo input
+    And presses Enter
+    Then the todo list contains 1 item
+    And the new-todo input is cleared
+    And the main section is visible
+    And the footer is visible
+
+  Scenario: User adds a todo with whitespace-only text
+    Given the app has loaded
+    When the user types "   " into the new-todo input
+    And presses Enter
+    Then the todo list is empty
+
+  Scenario: User adds a todo with trimmed text
+    Given the app has loaded
+    When the user types "  Buy groceries  " into the new-todo input
+    And presses Enter
+    Then the todo list contains 1 item with title "Buy groceries"
+
+  Scenario: Counter shows the number of active todos with correct pluralization
+    Given the app has loaded
+    When the user adds 1 active todo with title "Item one"
+    Then the todo-count shows "1 item left"
+    When the user adds 1 active todo with title "Item two"
+    Then the todo-count shows "2 items left"
+    When the user marks "Item one" as completed
+    Then the todo-count shows "1 item left"
+
+  Scenario: Clear completed button removes all completed todos
+    Given the app has loaded
+    When the user adds 2 active todos with titles "Task A" and "Task B"
+    And the user marks "Task A" as completed
+    Then the clear-completed button is visible
+    When the user clicks the clear-completed button
+    Then the todo list contains 1 item
+    And the todo list does not contain "Task A"
+    And the clear-completed button is not visible
+
+  Scenario: Clear completed button is hidden when there are no completed todos
+    Given the app has loaded
+    When the user adds 1 active todo with title "Only task"
+    Then the clear-completed button is not visible
\ No newline at end of file
diff --git a/features/todo-persistence.feature b/features/todo-persistence.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..8076e79
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/todo-persistence.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,39 @@
+Feature: Todo persistence
+  As a user
+  I want my todos to persist across page reloads
+  So that I do not lose my task list
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded fresh
+
+  Scenario: Todos are saved to localStorage
+    Given the app has loaded
+    When the user adds 1 active todo with title "Buy groceries"
+    Then localStorage contains a key matching "todos-"
+    And the stored value includes an item with title "Buy groceries"
+    And the stored value includes an item with id
+    And the stored item with title "Buy groceries" has completed set to false
+
+  Scenario: Completed state is persisted to localStorage
+    Given the app has loaded
+    When the user adds 1 active todo with title "Buy groceries"
+    And the user marks "Buy groceries" as completed
+    Then the stored item with title "Buy groceries" has completed set to true
+
+  Scenario: Todos are restored from localStorage on page load
+    Given that localStorage contains a saved todo with title "Buy groceries" that is not completed
+    When the page is reloaded
+    Then the todo list contains 1 item with title "Buy groceries"
+    And the todo item "Buy groceries" does not have class "completed"
+
+  Scenario: Editing state is not persisted
+    Given the app has loaded
+    When the user adds 1 active todo with title "Buy groceries"
+    And the user double-clicks the label for "Buy groceries"
+    And the page is reloaded immediately
+    Then the todo item "Buy groceries" does not have class "editing"
+
+  Scenario: Todos use correct data format
+    Given the app has loaded
+    When the user adds 1 active todo with title "Buy groceries"
+    Then the stored todo has keys "id", "title", and "completed"
\ No newline at end of file
diff --git a/features/todo-routing.feature b/features/todo-routing.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..560e744
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/todo-routing.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,39 @@
+Feature: Todo routing and filtering
+  As a user
+  I want to filter todos by completion status
+  So that I can focus on active or completed items
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app has loaded
+    When the user adds 3 active todos with titles "Alpha", "Beta", and "Gamma"
+    And the user marks "Beta" as completed
+
+  Scenario: Default route shows all todos
+    Given the app is at the default route "#/"
+    Then the todo list shows 3 items
+    And the "All" filter link has class "selected"
+
+  Scenario: Active route shows only active todos
+    When the user navigates to "#/active"
+    Then the todo list shows 2 items
+    And the "Active" filter link has class "selected"
+    And the displayed items are "Alpha" and "Gamma"
+
+  Scenario: Completed route shows only completed todos
+    When the user navigates to "#/completed"
+    Then the todo list shows 1 item
+    And the "Completed" filter link has class "selected"
+    And the displayed items are "Beta"
+
+  Scenario: Filter selection is persisted on reload
+    When the user navigates to "#/active"
+    And the page is reloaded
+    Then the "Active" filter link has class "selected"
+    And the todo list shows 2 items
+
+  Scenario: Toggling an item in a filtered view hides it
+    When the user navigates to "#/active"
+    Then the todo list shows 2 items
+    When the user marks "Alpha" as completed
+    Then the todo list shows 1 item
+    And the displayed items are "Gamma"
\ No newline at end of file
diff --git a/features/todo-toggling.feature b/features/todo-toggling.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..c3e3b8b
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/todo-toggling.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,43 @@
+Feature: Todo item toggling
+  As a user
+  I want to mark todos as complete or incomplete
+  So that I can track my progress
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app has loaded
+
+  Scenario: User marks a todo as completed by clicking its checkbox
+    Given the app has loaded
+    When the user adds 1 active todo with title "Buy groceries"
+    And the user clicks the toggle checkbox for "Buy groceries"
+    Then the todo item "Buy groceries" has class "completed"
+    And the todo item "Buy groceries" shows as checked
+
+  Scenario: Mark all as complete checkbox toggles all todos
+    Given the app has loaded
+    When the user adds 3 active todos with titles "A", "B", and "C"
+    And the user clicks the toggle-all checkbox
+    Then every todo item has class "completed"
+    And the toggle-all checkbox is checked
+
+  Scenario: Mark all as complete checkbox reflects individual toggles
+    Given the app has loaded
+    When the user adds 3 active todos with titles "A", "B", and "C"
+    And the user clicks the toggle checkbox for "A"
+    And the user clicks the toggle checkbox for "B"
+    And the user clicks the toggle checkbox for "C"
+    Then the toggle-all checkbox is checked
+
+  Scenario: Toggle-all checkbox is unchecked when not all todos are completed
+    Given the app has loaded
+    When the user adds 3 active todos with titles "A", "B", and "C"
+    And the user clicks the toggle checkbox for "A"
+    Then the toggle-all checkbox is not checked
+
+  Scenario: Clear completed resets toggle-all checkbox state
+    Given the app has loaded
+    When the user adds 3 active todos with titles "A", "B", and "C"
+    And the user clicks the toggle-all checkbox
+    And the user clicks the clear-completed button
+    Then the todo list is empty
+    And the toggle-all checkbox is not checked
